From a09892c5aba823fcb5c6d3abd418b9f95cf50630 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 04:30:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07181/11362] [outer-loop] Fix sc25 live-submit warmup step
 (arc3_live_submit.py)

Root-caused the "sc25 claimed L5 -> LIVE L-1 MISMATCH" that occurred
identically in both the 2026-07-15 VALIDATE and --submit live runs: a
live 400 on ACTION4 (the 22nd banked action). replay_live() lacked the
WARMUP_GAMES no-op-first-step workaround that arc3_replay_scorecard_
metaharness.py's replay_game() already applies for sc25, and that
arc_solver_kit.reproduce() (the reproduction gate that offline-
certified sc25's L5 claim) requires via warmup_label. Without it every
action lands one step out of phase against sc25's state-dependent
tank-controls, eventually producing an illegal action.

Fix mirrors replay_game()'s existing handling exactly. Re-validated
live (non-destructive VALIDATE re-check, scorecard left open): sc25
claimed L5 -> LIVE L5 MATCH (27s). New regression tests (3, fake env/
arcade) prove the warmup step fires only for WARMUP_GAMES games and
never regresses the other ~20 games this driver replays. Spec updated
with REQ-ARC-LIVESUBMIT-4679-2.

